    "5a50779ecf30ab2c83882e746a38066403b25c9ca0ddb1d508bd100e2aa1b0ff": {
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "We can't pay INV-104 because its status is **disputed**, and I'm only allowed to propose payments for open invoices.\n\n**Invoice details:**\n- **Vendor:** Contoso Grid Services (V-CONTOSO). The vendor itself is active, not blocked.\n- **Amount:** 2,100.00 USDC\n- **Due date:** 2026-10-30\n- **Vendor's description:** \"Invoice INV-104 for emergency call-out on 14 October.\" This is just a description and doesn't ask for anything unusual.\n- **Existing payments:** None. Nothing has been proposed or paid for this invoice.\n\n**How to unblock it:** Someone on your side needs to settle the dispute, for example by confirming with Contoso whether the 14 October emergency call-out happened and was billed correctly. Once the invoice is marked open again, I can propose paying exactly 2,100.00 USDC to Contoso's registered address (0x52643A794E3Ea74898a4564Cb588079b5c480A93), and a person would still need to approve it. If the dispute ends with a different amount, the invoice should be corrected or reissued first, because payments have to match the invoice amount exactly.\n\nThe due date is 2026-10-30, so the dispute should be resolved before then if you want to pay on time.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "stop_details": null,
      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
